WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.240
Hi, this is Dr. Jelena Trajkovic, CECS Department, Cal State Long Beach.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.440
Let's look at the functioning of 221 max on

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.780
the FPGA board. First and foremost, let's look once again over setup.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.200
So the USB cable is connected to the USB on your computer and

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.400
the little mini cable is connected to your FPGA board. Just be very careful not to force it in as

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:36.360
there is a right side and wrong side of this cable to go inside the slot and the

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:46.520
power is switched on. After programming the device using the XDC file we mapped

00:00:46.520 --> 00:01:07.820
input 1 to L16 and if input IN0 to J15 and leftmost switch which is V10 is

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:09.940
is actually going to be select signal.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:17.140
LED, which is connected to T15,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.540
is going to be on or off,

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.520
depending on what is on input.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:28.520
So here, we start by having everything in zero position.

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:33.540
So both our IN0 and IN1 are zero,

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.340
and my select signal is zero as well.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:45.860
If we flip IN1, we will see that the LED will show 1, because we are selecting this input

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.780
and this input has 1.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.860
How about selecting input 1?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.180
Input 1 is 0, our output is 0 as well.

00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:00.700
If we flip the switch, the output is going to change to 1.

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:04.940
If we change this value, nothing is going to change.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:08.580
And we can play like that and test all the possible inputs

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:13.580
and outputs of FPGA implementation of two to one max.

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.900
Congratulations, you made your first FPGA design.

